      "abstract": "Johann Gottlieb Fichte\u2019s thinking is part of the Sattelzeit, in which the foundation for the modern use of important concepts is laid. The stages of Fichte\u2019s philosophy and his various theories of religion and Christianity reflect attempts to determine the function of religion in a modern society. Important is the philosophical foundation of religion, which is transformed from a moral theology based on Kant to a unified theory of the philosophy of mind. Fichte thus offers an alternative to Hegel and Schelling. This alternative has only been taken up in Protestant theology at a small number of points, but all the more intensively.",
